<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēvectĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		eveho. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A going upwards</i>, <i>flying
			up</i>, <i>flight</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublimis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 169</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			jurid. lang., <i>a permit to travel by the public
			post</i>, <i>a post-warrant</i>, <i><span class="en">Cod.
					Just. 12, 51, 3 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep.
				4, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. Ep. 55</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
